IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mai-core`

-- Motor Accident Injuries Act 2019 (ACT) -- the defined benefits, from the seat of the relevant insurer.
--
-- SEAT: the relevant insurer for a motor accident (s 34): the CTP insurer of the vehicle, an interstate insurer, or the
-- nominal defendant. The Act puts hard duties on it: a receipt notice within the MAI guidelines' period (s 60), a
-- liability decision within 28 days or deemed acceptance (s 65), a response to a late application's explanation
-- within 28 days or deemed acceptance (s 59 (4)), payment (s 66) every 14 days (s 102), the WPI notice within 14 days
-- (ss 154-157), and the application to the ACAT for death benefits (s 176). It asks: "By when must I act? Am I taken
-- to have accepted? How much must I pay or offer? When may I apply to the ACAT?" The rules are in mai-core.l4; this
-- module builds the core's records from plain answers and restates no rule. Its names are its own: none is defined in
-- mai-seat.l4.
--
-- FIGURES: as in mai-seat.l4 (NI2026-402).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accident Injuries Act 2019 (ACT) -- the relevant insurer's questions`

GIVEN `accident`       IS A DATE
      `age`            IS A NUMBER
      `situation`      IS A `Work situation`
      `pension age`    IS A DATE
      `damages paid`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `disentitled`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Injured person's facts`
`the injured person's facts for the insurer` `accident` `age` `situation` `pension age` `damages paid` `disentitled` MEANS
    `Injured person's facts` WITH
        `date of the motor accident`                       IS `accident`
        `age on the date of the motor accident`            IS `age`
        `work situation on the date of the motor accident` IS `situation`
        `date the injured person reaches pension age`      IS `pension age`
        -- The insurer pays a living injured person; s 175 covers what the estate is owed.
        `the injured person has died`                      IS FALSE
        `an insurer has paid damages for loss of income under a motor accident claim` IS `damages paid`
        -- The insurer states one fact for division 2.2.2: whether a limitation in ss 43 (2), 44 to 50 ends the injured
        -- person's income replacement benefits. It is carried in the s 44 field, which the income replacement rule
        -- reads; the other fields are FALSE.
        `limitations` IS
            `Division 2.2.2 facts` WITH
                `s 43 (2): driver or responsible person of an uninsured vehicle, with no s 43 (2) exception` IS FALSE
                `s 43 (3): driver or responsible person of an uninsured vehicle, with no other insured vehicle whose insurer is the relevant insurer` IS FALSE
                `s 44: convicted or found guilty of a driving offence in relation to the accident` IS `disentitled`
                `s 45: convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences in relation to the accident` IS FALSE
                `s 46: the injury is intentionally self-inflicted` IS FALSE
                `s 47: a detainee or young detainee for the period` IS FALSE
                `s 48: convicted or found guilty of a serious offence in relation to the accident` IS FALSE
                `s 49: the MAI commission has notified that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism` IS FALSE
                `s 50: a workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled` IS FALSE

§§ `Applications (ss 59, 60, 65)`

@export By when must I give the applicant a receipt notice for the application for defined benefits (s 60 (1))?
GIVEN `the date I received the application` IS A DATE @desc The date you, the relevant insurer, received the application for defined benefits (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the days the MAI guidelines give me for a receipt notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days after receiving an application that the MAI guidelines allow for a receipt notice (the guidelines are not part of this encoding)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I give the receipt notice` IS
    `the last day for the receipt notice` `the date I received the application` `the days the MAI guidelines give me for a receipt notice`

@export By when must I decide whether I accept liability for the defined benefits, and give the applicant notice (s 65 (1))?
GIVEN `the date of the receipt notice I gave` IS A DATE @desc The date of the receipt notice (or late receipt notice) you gave the applicant (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I decide liability` IS
    `the last day to decide liability after a receipt notice on` `the date of the receipt notice I gave`

@export Have I accepted, or am I taken to have accepted, liability for the defined benefits (s 65 (2) to (4))?
GIVEN `the date of the receipt notice I gave` IS A DATE @desc The date of the receipt notice (or late receipt notice) you gave the applicant (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the notice I have given about liability` IS A `Decision on liability so far` @desc Which notice about liability you have given the applicant, if any: none yet, a defined benefits notice, a transfer notice or a rejection notice
      `the date of my notice` IS A DATE @desc The date you gave that notice (YYYY-MM-DD); if none, give today's date
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc The day asked about, usually today (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A `Liability position`
DECIDE `Am I taken to have accepted liability` IS
    `the s 65 liability position` `the date of the receipt notice I gave` `the notice I have given about liability` `the date of my notice` `the day in question`

@export May I accept this application as a late application, and am I taken to have accepted it because I did not respond to the explanation within 28 days (s 59 (2), (4), (5))?
GIVEN `the benefits applied for` IS A `Benefits applied for` @desc Which defined benefits the application is for: income replacement or treatment and care benefits, death benefits, or funeral benefits
      `the accident date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the death date` IS A DATE @desc For death or funeral benefits, the date the injured person died (YYYY-MM-DD); otherwise the accident date
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE @desc The date the application was made (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date I received the explanation for the delay` IS A DATE @desc The date you received the applicant's explanation for the late application (YYYY-MM-DD); for an application in time, the date of the application
      `my response to the explanation` IS A `Response to a late application` @desc Whether you have responded to the applicant about the explanation: no response yet, accepted, or refused
      `the date of my response` IS A DATE @desc The date you responded (YYYY-MM-DD); if you have not, give today's date
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc The day asked about, usually today (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH AN `Application timing`
DECIDE `May I accept the late application` IS
    `the s 59 timing of the application` `the benefits applied for` `the accident date` `the death date` `the date of the application` `the date I received the explanation for the delay` `my response to the explanation` `the date of my response` `the day in question`

§§ `Income replacement benefits (part 2.4)`

@export How much income replacement benefit must I pay the injured person for the week that includes this day, and for the fortnight (ss 96, 97, 98, 101, 102)?
GIVEN `the payment day` IS A DATE @desc A day in the week the payment is for (YYYY-MM-DD); the AWE indexed amounts of that day are used (deposited for 1 April 2026 to 31 March 2027)
      `the accident date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the injured person's age on the accident date` IS A NUMBER @desc The injured person's age in whole years on the date of the accident
      `the injured person's work situation on the accident date` IS A `Work situation` @desc The injured person's situation on the date of the accident, in the categories of ss 78 to 87
      `the date the injured person reaches pension age` IS A DATE @desc The date the injured person reaches, or reached, pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cwlth), s 23 (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `an insurer has paid the injured person damages for loss of income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an insurer has already paid the injured person damages for loss of income under a motor accident claim
      `a limitation in ss 43 to 50 ends the injured person's income replacement benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of ss 43 (2), 44, 45, 46, 47, 48, 49 or 50 ends or excludes the injured person's income replacement benefits for this period
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE @desc The date the application for defined benefits was made (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I am satisfied there are exceptional circumstances for earlier payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a late application, whether you are satisfied on reasonable grounds that exceptional circumstances justify paying from the earlier date (no if the application was in time)
      `the date the injured person expected to return to or start work` IS A DATE @desc For a person on unpaid leave, with a new work arrangement, or a full-time student: the date they expected to return to paid work or start work or a business (YYYY-MM-DD); otherwise the accident date
      `the injured person's pre-injury income, AWE adjusted` IS A NUMBER @desc The injured person's pre-injury weekly income or earning capacity (ss 80 to 88), AWE adjusted (s 94), in Australian dollars a week
      `the post-injury earning capacity I have decided` IS A NUMBER @desc The injured person's post-injury earning capacity as you decided it under s 100, in Australian dollars a week
      `an employer paid superannuation for the injured person in the 52 weeks before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an employer paid, or had to pay, superannuation contributions for the injured person in the 52 weeks before the accident
      `the SG charge percentage for that year` IS A NUMBER @desc The superannuation guarantee charge percentage for the year the contributions were paid or payable, which s 96 (2) takes from the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 (Cwlth), s 19 (2) (12 for 2025-26; from 1 July 2026 that Act sets 12 in s 17A (2))
      `the workers compensation the injured person receives for that week` IS A NUMBER @desc Any weekly workers compensation payment for loss of income the injured person receives for that week, in Australian dollars
GIVETH AN `Income replacement answer`
DECIDE `How much income replacement benefit must I pay` IS
    `the income replacement benefit for the week of` `the payment day` `for` (`the injured person's facts for the insurer` `the accident date` `the injured person's age on the accident date` `the injured person's work situation on the accident date` `the date the injured person reaches pension age` `an insurer has paid the injured person damages for loss of income` `a limitation in ss 43 to 50 ends the injured person's income replacement benefits`) (`Application facts` WITH
        `date of the application`                                                    IS `the date of the application`
        `the insurer is satisfied on reasonable grounds that exceptional circumstances justify earlier payment` IS `I am satisfied there are exceptional circumstances for earlier payment`
        `date the person anticipated returning to paid work, or starting work or a business` IS `the date the injured person expected to return to or start work`) (`Income replacement figures` WITH
        `pre-injury income AWE adjusted`                                        IS `the injured person's pre-injury income, AWE adjusted`
        `post-injury earning capacity`                                          IS `the post-injury earning capacity I have decided`
        `employer superannuation contributions paid or payable in the 52 weeks before the accident` IS `an employer paid superannuation for the injured person in the 52 weeks before`
        `superannuation guarantee charge percentage for the year of the contributions` IS `the SG charge percentage for that year`
        `workers compensation payment for the week`                             IS `the workers compensation the injured person receives for that week`)

@export For what period must I pay the injured person income replacement benefits (s 101)?
GIVEN `the accident date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the injured person's age on the accident date` IS A NUMBER @desc The injured person's age in whole years on the date of the accident
      `the injured person's work situation on the accident date` IS A `Work situation` @desc The injured person's situation on the date of the accident, in the categories of ss 78 to 87
      `the date the injured person reaches pension age` IS A DATE @desc The date the injured person reaches, or reached, pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cwlth), s 23 (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `an insurer has paid the injured person damages for loss of income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an insurer has already paid the injured person damages for loss of income under a motor accident claim
      `a limitation in ss 43 to 50 ends the injured person's income replacement benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of ss 43 (2), 44, 45, 46, 47, 48, 49 or 50 ends or excludes the injured person's income replacement benefits
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE @desc The date the application for defined benefits was made (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I am satisfied there are exceptional circumstances for earlier payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a late application, whether you are satisfied on reasonable grounds that exceptional circumstances justify paying from the earlier date (no if the application was in time)
      `the date the injured person expected to return to or start work` IS A DATE @desc For a person on unpaid leave, with a new work arrangement, or a full-time student: the date they expected to return to paid work or start work or a business (YYYY-MM-DD); otherwise the accident date
GIVETH A `Period answer`
DECIDE `For what period must I pay income replacement benefits` IS
    `the period for which income replacement benefits are payable` (`the injured person's facts for the insurer` `the accident date` `the injured person's age on the accident date` `the injured person's work situation on the accident date` `the date the injured person reaches pension age` `an insurer has paid the injured person damages for loss of income` `a limitation in ss 43 to 50 ends the injured person's income replacement benefits`) (`Application facts` WITH
        `date of the application`                                                    IS `the date of the application`
        `the insurer is satisfied on reasonable grounds that exceptional circumstances justify earlier payment` IS `I am satisfied there are exceptional circumstances for earlier payment`
        `date the person anticipated returning to paid work, or starting work or a business` IS `the date the injured person expected to return to or start work`)

@export How much may I pay the injured person as an interim weekly payment while I wait for information I asked for (s 103)?
GIVEN `the accident date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date I asked for the additional information` IS A DATE @desc The date you asked the injured person for additional information to decide the amount of income replacement benefits (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the injured person has given me the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person has given you the information
      `the date it was given` IS A DATE @desc The date the information was given (YYYY-MM-DD); if not given, today's date
      `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of $2 250 AWE indexed prescribed by regulation for an interim weekly payment (not part of this encoding), for example 80
      `the payment day` IS A DATE @desc The day the payment is for (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A `MAI amount answer`
DECIDE `How much interim weekly payment may I pay` IS
    `the interim weekly payment` `the prescribed percentage` `on` `the payment day` `ending` (`the last day for interim weekly payments` `the accident date` `the date I asked for the additional information` `the injured person has given me the information` `the date it was given`)

§§ `Quality of life benefits (part 2.6) -- once the WPI report is in`

@export Which WPI notice must I give the injured person, and must I make an offer (ss 154 to 157)?
GIVEN `the injured person's WPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The injured person's WPI as a whole number percentage, from the WPI report (the higher one if physical and psychological injuries were assessed separately)
      `the injured person is entitled to make a motor accident claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person is entitled to make a motor accident claim (someone is liable to them in damages for the injury)
GIVETH A `WPI notice section`
DECIDE `Which WPI notice must I give` IS
    `the WPI notice section for` `the injured person's WPI` `the injured person is entitled to make a motor accident claim`

@export By when must I give the injured person the WPI notice (ss 154 (3), 155 (4), 156 (4), 157 (4))?
GIVEN `the date I received the WPI report` IS A DATE @desc The date you received the WPI report (the later one if physical and psychological injuries were reported on separately) (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I give the WPI notice` IS
    `the last day for the WPI notice` `the date I received the WPI report`

@export How much quality of life benefit must I offer for the injured person's WPI (s 167, table 167)?
GIVEN `the injured person's WPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The injured person's WPI as a whole number percentage, from the WPI report (the higher one if physical and psychological injuries were assessed separately)
      `the date of the WPI report` IS A DATE @desc The date of the WPI report (the later one if separate; or of the notice of affirmation or increase on review) (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the injured person was a child at the accident and is taken to have 10% WPI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person was a child at the accident and, 4 years and 6 months after it, was receiving treatment and care benefits meeting the prescribed requirements or was an LTCS participant (s 133)
      `a limitation in ss 43 to 50 ends the injured person's quality of life benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of ss 43 (3), 44, 45, 46, 48, 49 or 50 ends or excludes the injured person's quality of life benefits
      `the injured person is a foreign national living permanently outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person is neither an Australian citizen nor a permanent resident and lives permanently outside Australia (s 134)
      `the injured person has already received quality of life benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person has already received quality of life benefits for the accident (s 135)
      `the injured person has been awarded quality of life damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person has been awarded quality of life damages in a motor accident claim for the accident (s 136)
GIVETH A `MAI amount answer`
DECIDE `How much quality of life benefit must I offer` IS
    `the quality of life benefits payable` (`Quality of life facts` WITH
        `WPI assessed`                                                   IS `the injured person's WPI`
        `a child on the date of the motor accident`                      IS `the injured person was a child at the accident and is taken to have 10% WPI`
        `4 years 6 months after the accident, receiving treatment and care benefits and meeting the prescribed requirements, or an LTCS scheme participant` IS `the injured person was a child at the accident and is taken to have 10% WPI`
        `a foreign national living permanently outside Australia`        IS `the injured person is a foreign national living permanently outside Australia`
        `has already received quality of life benefits for the accident` IS `the injured person has already received quality of life benefits`
        `has been awarded quality of life damages for the accident`      IS `the injured person has been awarded quality of life damages`
        -- The insurer states one fact for division 2.2.2, carried in the s 44 field, which the quality of life rule
        -- reads; the other fields are FALSE.
        `limitations` IS
            `Division 2.2.2 facts` WITH
                `s 43 (2): driver or responsible person of an uninsured vehicle, with no s 43 (2) exception` IS FALSE
                `s 43 (3): driver or responsible person of an uninsured vehicle, with no other insured vehicle whose insurer is the relevant insurer` IS FALSE
                `s 44: convicted or found guilty of a driving offence in relation to the accident` IS `a limitation in ss 43 to 50 ends the injured person's quality of life benefits`
                `s 45: convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences in relation to the accident` IS FALSE
                `s 46: the injury is intentionally self-inflicted` IS FALSE
                `s 47: a detainee or young detainee for the period` IS FALSE
                `s 48: convicted or found guilty of a serious offence in relation to the accident` IS FALSE
                `s 49: the MAI commission has notified that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism` IS FALSE
                `s 50: a workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled` IS FALSE) `the date of the WPI report`

§§ `Death and funeral benefits (parts 2.7, 2.8) -- after a death`

@export From what day may I apply to the ACAT for the order for payment of the death benefits, which I must then make (s 176)?
GIVEN `the date I accepted liability for the death benefits` IS A DATE @desc The date you accepted liability for the application for death benefits (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `ACT public holidays on weekdays in the 5 business days after` IS A NUMBER @desc How many ACT public holidays fall on a weekday in the business days counted after that date (usually 0)
      `I gave a dependant notice asking for additional information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave a dependant notice asking for additional information about the application
      `the date of that notice to the dependant` IS A DATE @desc The date of that notice (YYYY-MM-DD); if none, the date you accepted liability
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From when may I apply to the ACAT` IS
    `the first day the insurer may apply to the ACAT` `the date I accepted liability for the death benefits` `ACT public holidays on weekdays in the 5 business days after` `I gave a dependant notice asking for additional information` `the date of that notice to the dependant`

-- The death facts as the insurer states them. The s 169 (2) exclusions are one fact, carried in the s 173 field,
-- which the exclusion rule reads; the other exclusion fields are FALSE.
GIVEN `accident`  IS A DATE
      `death`     IS A DATE
      `partner`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `children`  IS A NUMBER
      `excluded`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Death facts`
`the death facts for the insurer` `accident` `death` `partner` `children` `excluded` MEANS
    `Death facts` WITH
        `date of the motor accident`                                          IS `accident`
        `date of death`                                                       IS `death`
        `had a domestic partner or dependent former domestic partner on the date of the motor accident` IS `partner`
        `number of dependent children on the date of the motor accident`      IS `children`
        `the death was caused by an intentionally self-inflicted injury`      IS FALSE
        `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism` IS FALSE
        `a foreign national whose death happened outside Australia`           IS FALSE
        `a coroner established conduct making up 2 or more driving offences or a serious offence` IS FALSE
        `the person who died received quality of life benefits or damages`    IS FALSE
        `death benefits were paid under a workers compensation scheme`        IS `excluded`

@export What is the most the ACAT can order me to pay in death benefits for these dependants (ss 174, 177 (2))?
GIVEN `the accident date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date the person died` IS A DATE @desc The date the person died (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the person had a domestic partner or dependent former domestic partner at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the date of the accident, the person who died had a domestic partner or a financially dependent former domestic partner
      `the person's dependent children at the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children (s 168 (2)) the person who died had on the date of the accident
      `an exclusion in s 46, 49 or 170 to 173 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of the exclusions in s 46 (2), 49, 170, 171, 172 or 173 applies to the death benefits
      `the day of the ACAT order` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the death benefits are worked out, for example the date of the ACAT order (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A `MAI amount answer`
DECIDE `What is the most the ACAT can order me to pay in death benefits` IS
    `the death benefits payable to the dependants` (`the death facts for the insurer` `the accident date` `the date the person died` `the person had a domestic partner or dependent former domestic partner at the accident` `the person's dependent children at the accident` `an exclusion in s 46, 49 or 170 to 173 applies`) `the day of the ACAT order`

@export Is an ACAT order for this total amount of death benefits within the s 177 (2) cap?
GIVEN `the accident date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date the person died` IS A DATE @desc The date the person died (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the person had a domestic partner or dependent former domestic partner at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the date of the accident, the person who died had a domestic partner or a financially dependent former domestic partner
      `the person's dependent children at the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children (s 168 (2)) the person who died had on the date of the accident
      `an exclusion in s 46, 49 or 170 to 173 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of the exclusions in s 46 (2), 49, 170, 171, 172 or 173 applies to the death benefits
      `the day of the ACAT order` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the death benefits are worked out, for example the date of the ACAT order (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the total the order would require me to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The total death benefits, for all dependants, that the order would require you to pay, in Australian dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the ACAT order within the cap` IF
    `the ACAT order is within the s 177 (2) cap` (`the death facts for the insurer` `the accident date` `the date the person died` `the person had a domestic partner or dependent former domestic partner at the accident` `the person's dependent children at the accident` `an exclusion in s 46, 49 or 170 to 173 applies`) `the day of the ACAT order` `the total the order would require me to pay`

@export Must I pay the estate the income replacement and treatment and care benefits the person was owed when they died, and give up recovering what I paid (s 175)?
GIVEN `I have accepted liability for an application for death benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have accepted liability for an application for death benefits for the person who died
      `the person was entitled to income replacement or treatment and care benefits before dying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before dying, the person was entitled to income replacement benefits or treatment and care benefits
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I pay the estate what the person was owed` IF
    `the estate must be paid the benefits owed and not received, and nothing paid is recovered (s 175)` `I have accepted liability for an application for death benefits` `the person was entitled to income replacement or treatment and care benefits before dying`

@export What is the most I must pay in funeral benefits for these funeral expenses (ss 178 to 181)?
GIVEN `the accident date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date the person died` IS A DATE @desc The date the person died (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the funeral expenses claimed` IS A NUMBER @desc The funeral expenses the applicant has paid or is liable to pay, as the MAI guidelines allow, in Australian dollars
      `an exclusion in s 49, 179 or 180 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 49 (terrorism), s 179 (a foreign national who died outside Australia) or s 180 (funeral expenses paid under a workers compensation scheme) applies
      `the payment date` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the funeral benefits are worked out or paid (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A `MAI amount answer`
DECIDE `What must I pay in funeral benefits` IS
    `the funeral benefits payable` (`Funeral facts` WITH
        `date of the motor accident`                                          IS `the accident date`
        `date of death`                                                       IS `the date the person died`
        -- The applicant for funeral benefits is the person who has paid, or is liable to pay, the expenses (s 178 (1)).
        `has paid, or is liable to pay, the funeral expenses`                 IS TRUE
        `the funeral expenses`                                                IS `the funeral expenses claimed`
        -- One fact for the exclusions, carried in the s 180 field; the others are FALSE.
        `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism` IS FALSE
        `a foreign national whose death happened outside Australia`           IS FALSE
        `funeral expenses were paid under a workers compensation scheme`      IS `an exclusion in s 49, 179 or 180 applies`) `the payment date`
